  "title": "SPEC-MAT-002B — Inventory, Lot/Container & Warehouse Events",
  "description": "Document 113 event contract for the events app/modules/material/commands.py actually emits for Document 20. 6 of the catalogue's 9 declared events are implemented: InventoryTransferred, InventoryReserved, InventoryReservationReleased, ContainerSplit, ContainerMerged, InventoryAdjusted (mutually exclusive with the undeclared InventoryCounted on the same call site, chosen by whether the count delta is non-zero). InventoryReceived, MaterialQualityHoldPlaced and InventoryERPDiscrepancyDetected are declared but have no producing code path -- initial receipt into inventory is covered by Document 19's MaterialReceived/MaterialLotReceived rather than a separate InventoryReceived event, quality holds are covered by MaterialQuarantined (Document 19) rather than a distinct inventory-side hold event, and ERP inventory-discrepancy detection is not yet built. Verified directly against source.",
